<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis I, Duke of Nevers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1516">1516</a>–<a href="/years/1561">1561</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as François de Clèves, François I de Clèves</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis I, Duke of Nevers, born François de Clèves, was a French nobleman and soldier of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>, which had held the county of Nevers since 1491. In 1539 Francis I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> raised Nevers to a duchy-peerage for him, making him its first duke. He served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> and Henry II in their wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, and through his daughter Henriette the duchy later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga family</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-i-duke-of-nevers.jpg" alt="Francis I, Duke of Nevers" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of François Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francis_I_of_Cleves,_duke_of_Nevers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
